Z||000000||Master_Sushi||11-16-2001||02:42 PM||||I tired everything but my 84se is staying at 2-3k rpm all the time. I checked my vacume lines and made sure they arn't leaking. I read through the archives and didn't find anything that fixed it. Any tips? Only things I haven't done is started to replace all my sensors. This is my winter beater I don't want to spend to much money one it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||11-16-2001||03:48 PM||||Check your egr valve.  My 84 keeps letting the valve work loose every few months.  When it gets loose the idle gets funky||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||11-16-2001||06:01 PM||||Ok, I fixed this today! Happy Happy Joy Joy! Was an interesting fix. I knew my lines wern't leaking, all my sensors were good also because they looked quite new. What I did was take the IAC out and unscrewed the nub on the end about 3mm. My idel was WAY to low after that I could barley keep the engine runing. I took it out again and adjusted it again for a total of 1mm out of normal. Idel is prefect and at 900rpm all the time. I don't think this is ment to be adjusted but it worked great!!! I haven't read about this anwhere on the forum so I wrote this out just FYI... My cars runing like a champ now!||||reg||4
